# Local overrides for `pnpm --filter @tcg/annotation dev`. Copy to `.env.local`.
#
# The root `.env.example` is the one a new developer copies to start the whole
# stack; this file exists because Next reads env files from the app directory,
# not the repository root. Keep the two in step — `tests/test_environment_example.py`
# fails if a variable here is missing from the root example.
#
# Every variable is validated by `lib/env.ts`: unset falls back to the default
# below, but a malformed value throws rather than failing later as an
# unexplained fetch error.

# Base URL of the FastAPI service (services/api), as reachable from the
# browser. Must be an absolute http/https URL. Falls back to
# http://localhost:8000 when unset. `NEXT_PUBLIC_` values are inlined into the
# browser bundle — never put a secret here.
#
# This is the only variable the tool reads, and that is load-bearing rather
# than minimal: `tests/no-object-store.test.ts` asserts it, because an
# application that knows one origin cannot reach an object store behind its
# back.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
